 ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-ndt-2-247">b</xref></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28%</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02013;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02013;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn1-ndt-2-247"><label>a</label><p>Conclusions reached by study authors based on consideration of all primary and secondary efficacy outcomes, including those not summarized here.</p></fn><fn id="tfn2-ndt-2-247"><label>b</label><p>Primary efficacy measure.</p></fn><fn id="tfn3-ndt-2-247"><label>c</label><p>p &#x02264; 0.005 vs placebo.</p></fn><fn id="tfn4-ndt-2-247"><label>d</label><p>p &#x02264; 0.05 vs placebo.</p></fn><fn id="tfn5-ndt-2-247"><label>e</label><p>p &#x02264; 0.05 vs comparator.</p></fn><fn id="tfn6-ndt-2-247"><label>f</label><p>Nonsignificant difference vs comparator (p&#x0003e;0.05).</p></fn><fn id="tfn7-ndt-2-247"><label>g</label><p>Comparison of all functional disability categories combined.</p></fn><fn id="tfn8-ndt-2-247"><label>h</label><p>p &#x0003c; 0.05 vs rizatriptan 5 mg.</p></fn><fn id="tfn9-ndt-2-247"><label>i</label><p>p &#x02264; 0.005 vs comparator.</p></fn><fn id="tfn10-ndt-2-247"><p>Brackets indicate treatment groups compared in statistical analyses.</p></fn><fn id="tfn11-ndt-2-247"><p><bold>Abbreviations:</bold> CO, cross over; E/C, ergotamine&#x02013;caffeine; n, patients who took study medication; N, naratriptan; PG, parallel group; PC, placebo-controlled; R, rizatriptan; S, sumatriptan; Z, zolmitriptan.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t2-ndt-2-247" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Efficacy of rizatriptan in the acute treatment of migraine in retrospective analyses of comparative studies</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">Proportion of patients achieving efficacy measures, % (odds rati